{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"1e4a25d1-1a18-440c-b187-37f563f41050","step_index":28,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"{\"divergences\":[{\"requirementId\":\"REQ-03-3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"Mandatory deployment-tooling verification of official target-chain USDC quote-token address is absent from repository scope\"}],\"documentProblems\":[\"IRaffleFactory.sol:L8-L9 states that 'onchain construction checks only code presence and six-decimal metadata', whereas RaffleFactory.constructor (RaffleFactory.sol:L68, L80-L83, L89-L90) and Raffle.constructor (Raffle.sol:L157 -\\u003e VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol:L45) also validate protocolTreasury_ against zero and protocol plumbing addresses and invoke vrfWrapper_.link() during construction.\",\"IRaffleFactory.sol:L89, IRaffle.sol:L266, RaffleFactory.sol:L152, and Raffle.sol:L587-L589 describe _isProtocolDestination and UnsafeProtocolDestination as screening tokens, ticket owners, and payout recipients against known protocol plumbing, omitting that Raffle.initialize (Raffle.sol:L187-L192) also screens params.sponsor (which receives neither tickets nor payouts) and params.protocolTreasury against params.prizeToken and registered clones.\",\"DESIGN.md:L2 states 'Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. ... Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss' without specifying the rounding direction of the 80% cash-winner allocation before computing the sponsor remainder, whereas IRaffle.sol:L328, Raffle.sol:L529-L530, and RaffleConstants.sol:L7-L8 specify that both the 5% protocol fee and 80% cash-winner allocation round down via Math.mulDiv and the sponsor receives the remainder.\"],\"reportFile\":\"spec-compliance/REPORT.md\"}\n","duration_seconds":26.313541,"usage":{"input_tokens":106044,"output_tokens":580,"thinking_tokens":132,"cache_read_tokens":7019,"total_tokens":106624}}}
